184 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 109 0 R
/E (   To counter these psychological pressures we must move from passive scrolling to active management of our digital habits. This shift is most critical during the margins of our day those sensitive windows immediately after waking and right before sleep. When the brain is most vulnerable to social comparison immediately after waking and right before sleep. Create a strict rule that disallows you to look at the screen for the first 60 minutes of the day and the last 60 minutes before bed. This allows your mind to ground itself in your own reality before engaging with the specially selected lives of others.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [0]
>>
