231 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 115 0 R
/E (    The phenomenon of "doomscrolling" represents a profound shift in how humans process information, where the act of endlessly consuming negative digital content begins to fundamentally rewire our psychological resilience. This behavior is deeply rooted in an evolutionary mechanism known as the negativity bias, which originally served to keep our ancestors alert to physical threats but has now been hijacked by the infinite nature of social media feeds. Because our brains are biologically programmed to prioritize survival information over positive data, we find ourselves trapped in a loop of seeking out distressing news under the misplaced belief that "knowing more" equates to being safer.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
