234 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 116 0 R
/T (   This evolutionary trap leads directly into a physiological state of chronic hyper-vigilance, as the constant stream of crisis imagery triggers a persistent release of cortisol and adrenaline. Unlike a physical threat that eventually passes, the digital world offers no resolution, keeping the amygdala in a state of permanent alarm. )
/E (   This evolutionary trap leads directly into a physiological state of chronic hyper-vigilance, as the constant stream of crisis imagery triggers a persistent release of cortisol and adrenaline. Unlike a physical threat that eventually passes, the digital world offers no resolution, keeping the amygdala in a state of permanent alarm. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
235 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
