/E (   A study from the University of Pennsylvania showed people who cut social media down to half an hour each day felt less lonely and less depressed. Imagine realizing this - what we turn to for connection ends up pushing us further into isolation. Much like quenching thirst with seawater, it seems helpful at first, yet deepens the issue. The very act meant to bring closeness does quite the opposite.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [4]
>>
