/E (Scrolling through feeds eats into moments meant for actual people, while quietly twisting self-perception. Research appearing in the Journal of Social and Clinical Psychology showed clear harm: more platform time led to lower mood, fueled by comparing oneself to others. Instead of simply seeing vacation images, a person silently stacks their everyday against edited snapshots far removed from truth.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [3]
