/T (   A study by Hunt and team in 2018 looked at how cutting back on social media affects mood. Instead of scrolling endlessly, participants who limited their time felt less lonely. Because they spent fewer hours online, symptoms of depression dropped. Although it might seem small, simply reducing usage made a noticeable difference. When people engaged more offline, emotional well-being improved. )
/E (   A study by Hunt and team in 2018 looked at how cutting back on social media affects mood. Instead of scrolling endlessly, participants who limited their time felt less lonely. Because they spent fewer hours online, symptoms of depression dropped. Although it might seem small, simply reducing usage made a noticeable difference. When people engaged more offline, emotional well-being improved. )
